# Trivy CVE exception list — Gap 19
# Seventh AI Vision — accepted/deferred vulnerability exceptions
#
# Format (one exception per block):
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#   exp:YYYY-MM-DD      <- mandatory expiry; exception auto-expires, CI picks it up again
#   reason: <free text> <- mandatory justification for the record
#
# Rules:
#   1. Every entry MUST have an expiry date (exp:). No permanent exceptions.
#   2. Every entry MUST have a documented reason.
#   3. Entries are reviewed in the monthly security triage meeting.
#   4. Expired entries are removed; if still unpatched a tracker ticket is required.
#
# Add entries only when ALL of these conditions are true:
#   a) No upstream fix is available yet
#   b) The attack vector is not reachable in our deployment topology
#   c) A compensating control exists (e.g. network policy blocks the exploitable port)
#   d) A tracker ticket is open with the upstream maintainer or our security team
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Active exceptions (none at initial release — start clean)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Example (DO NOT REMOVE — reference for security team):
# CVE-2023-12345
# exp:2026-12-31
# reason: Affects only the FTP server component; this image has no FTP service.
#         Upstream fix expected in next minor release. Tracker: SEC-0042.
